  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "All L1 gold contexts report absolute oral bioavailability at or above 24% or describe F as high or excellent, including maraviroc 24 to 33%, silodosin 32.2%, odanacatib 30%, thalidomide 80 to 100%, tramadol 68%, aprepitant 59 to 67%, bitopertin high, dutasteride about 60%, and vicriviroc excellent; none affirmatively supports F below 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C01","C02","C03","C04","C05","C06","C07","C08","C09","C10","C11","C12","C13","C14","C17","C18","C19","C20"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The closest structural context, aprepitant, shares the 3,5-bis(trifluoromethyl)phenyl ether motif with the query and has measured human absolute F of 59 to 67% at 80 and 125 mg fasted, including geometric mean F 0.59 with 95% CI 0.53 to 0.65 for the 125 mg capsule.",
      "card_ids": ["C02","C08","C10","C12","C35"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 hepatic clearance records do not measure the query. The only analog-related record, aprepitant UGT1A4 CLint of 28 µl/min/µg protein, documents a metabolic pathway but does not imply low F because aprepitant absolute F is 59 to 67%.",
      "card_ids": ["C82"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Other L6 records concern unrelated molecules such as compound 45, phenobarbital, mephenytoin, PF-04445597, fluoxetine, and ipratropium; their intrinsic clearance or metabolic half-life values are not transferable to the query without structural or experimental support.",
      "card_ids": ["C73","C74","C75","C76","C77","C78","C79","C80","C81","C83","C84"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "No L6 record provides affirmative threshold-relevant evidence of hepatic first-pass loss sufficient to place the query below 20% absolute oral bioavailability.",
      "card_ids": ["C73","C74","C75","C76","C77","C78","C79","C80","C81","C82","C83","C84"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "hepatic_clearance_metabolic_stability",
      "applicability": "low",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C73","C74","C75","C76","C77","C78","C79","C80","C81","C82","C83","C84"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement for the query molecule is available in any level.",
    "No query-specific hepatic clearance or metabolic stability data exist; all L6 records are for other molecules.",
    "The aprepitant UGT1A4 record is for the structural analog, not the query, and aprepitant itself has high F.",
    "Query dose, formulation, and prandial state are unspecified; aprepitant F values are formulation-dependent.",
    "The low neutral fraction of 0.06 and high logD of 4.49 are physicochemical priors only and are not experimentally confirmed for the query.",
    "No matched IV comparator for the query is available, so L3 exposure values cannot be converted into absolute F estimates."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high is kept. All L1 gold contexts report F at or above 24% or describe F as high or excellent, the closest structural context aprepitant has human absolute F of 59 to 67%, and L6 hepatic clearance records provide no affirmative evidence of high first-pass loss for the query. The aprepitant UGT1A4 record shows metabolism but does not lower its measured F. Confidence remains moderate because no query-specific measurement exists."
}

